Quantifying Uncertainty in Analytical Measurement — Eurachem/CITAC (@met-quam: 0, is #book, #part-of @met-sources) { r_41N1P8BNZH26X9679RHB0THQNS
S. L. R. Ellison and A. Williams, editors. Eurachem/CITAC Guide: Quantifying Uncertainty in Analytical Measurement, third edition, 2012. ISBN 978-0-948926-30-3. [Official guide, translations, download, and errata](https://www.eurachem.org/index.php/publications/guides/quam).

Read the complete main treatment and selected worked examples during the chemical measurement branch, then all examples for advanced analytical study. Consult the publisher’s errata when a reconstructed numerical result differs. Earlier translations, including a Portuguese translation of the second edition, are identified separately and should not be cited as the 2012 third edition.

Use it to compare component-by-component uncertainty with evidence from validation and quality control. Keep the analytical method, sampling target, recovery treatment, and concentration basis explicit.

The publisher offers a free authorized PDF and retains copyright and translation/reproduction policies. Publication, edition, contents summary, and errata availability checked on 28 October 2026. External reference only.

